/** @page xmlusermodules User Modules

    @tableofcontents

    The following user modules are delivered and installed with the xml module. Each has its own documentation,
    including its release notes; load a module with \c %%requires and its name.

    @section xmlusermoduleswebservices SOAP and WSDL

    @subsection xmlusermoduleswsdl WSDL

    @ref wsdlintro "WSDL" parses WSDL 1.1 documents and their XML schemas into a model of
    the service (@ref WSDL::WebService "WebService"), and serializes and parses the SOAP 1.1, SOAP 1.2, HTTP and
    MIME messages of its operations, including faults, headers, attachments, MTOM/XOP packages and WS-Addressing
    headers. The other SOAP modules are built on it; it can also be used on its own to build or parse messages
    without a transport (see @ref xmlcookbooksoapmessage).

    @subsection xmlusermodulessoapclient SoapClient and SoapClientIo

    @ref soapclientiointro "SoapClientIo" (@ref SoapClientIo::SoapClientIo "SoapClientIo", connection schemes \c soapio and
    \c soapios) is the recommended SOAP client: it uses asynchronous I/O with HTTP/3, HTTP/2 or HTTP/1.1 and
    connection pooling. @ref soapclientintro "SoapClient" (@ref SoapClient::SoapClient "SoapClient", connection
    schemes \c soap and \c soaps) provides the same calls with the synchronous \c HTTPClient API. Both call the
    operations of a WSDL service by name with %Qore data and return the decoded response, raise SOAP faults as
    exceptions, and support SOAP header processing, MTOM/XOP, WS-Addressing, message limits and SOAP 1.2 \c GET
    retrieval. See @ref xmlcookbooksoap.

    @subsection xmlusermodulessoaphandler SoapHandler

    @ref soaphandlerintro "SoapHandler" (@ref SoapHandler::SoapHandler "SoapHandler") serves the operations of one or
    more WSDL services from the %Qore \c HttpServer: requests are validated and decoded, dispatched to %Qore
    callbacks, and the results or faults are serialized for the binding's SOAP version. See @ref xmlcookbooksoap.

    @subsection xmlusermodulessoapdataprovider SoapDataProvider

    @ref soapdataproviderintro "SoapDataProvider" (@ref SoapDataProvider::SoapDataProvider "SoapDataProvider", factory \c soap)
    exposes the operations of a SOAP service through the data provider API: each operation is a child provider with
    its request and response types, which can send requests to the server.

    @subsection xmlusermodulessalesforce SalesforceSoapClient

    @ref salesforcesoapclientintro "SalesforceSoapClient" (@ref SalesforceSoapClient::SalesforceSoapClient "SalesforceSoapClient",
    connection schemes \c sfsoap and \c sfsoaps) is a SOAP client for the Salesforce SOAP APIs that logs in and
    manages the session.

    @section xmlusermoduleswebdav WebDAV

    @subsection xmlusermoduleswebdavhandler WebDavHandler

    @ref webdavhandlerintro "WebDavHandler" provides WebDAV servers for the %Qore
    \c HttpServer: @ref WebDavHandler::FsWebDavHandler "FsWebDavHandler" serves a directory tree, and @ref WebDavHandler::AbstractWebDavHandler "AbstractWebDavHandler" is the base class for
    custom resource stores, with pluggable property and lock handlers. See @ref xmlwebdavguide.

    @subsection xmlusermoduleswebdavclient WebDavClient and WebDavClientIo

    @ref webdavclientiointro "WebDavClientIo" (@ref WebDavClientIo::WebDavClientIo "WebDavClientIo", connection schemes
    \c webdavio and \c webdavios) is the recommended WebDAV client, using asynchronous I/O;
    @ref webdavclientintro "WebDavClient" (@ref WebDavClient::WebDavClient "WebDavClient", connection schemes \c webdav and
    \c webdavs) provides the same API with the synchronous \c HTTPClient class. See @ref xmlcookbookwebdav.

    @subsection xmlusermoduleswebdavdp WebDavClientDataProvider

    @ref webdavclientdataproviderintro "WebDavClientDataProvider" (factory \c webdav)
    provides data provider actions for WebDAV resources: list, get, put, delete, mkdir, copy and move.

    @section xmlusermodulesxmlrpc XML-RPC

    - @ref xmlrpcclientiointro "XmlRpcClientIo" (@ref XmlRpcClientIo::XmlRpcClientIo "XmlRpcClientIo", connection schemes
      \c xmlrpcio and \c xmlrpcios): the recommended XML-RPC client, using asynchronous I/O
    - @ref xmlrpcconnectionintro "XmlRpcConnection" (connection schemes \c xmlrpc and
      \c xmlrpcs): connections for the native \c XmlRpcClient class
    - @ref xmlrpchandlerintro "XmlRpcHandler" (@ref XmlRpcHandler::XmlRpcHandler "XmlRpcHandler"): an XML-RPC server handler
      for the %Qore \c HttpServer

    See @ref xmlrpcguide.

    @section xmlusermodulesdataproviders XML Data Providers

    - @ref saxdataproviderintro "SaxDataProvider" (factories \c sax and \c saxwrite): reads
      the records of large XML documents with SAX iteration, and writes records as XML
    - @ref cargoxmldataproviderintro "CargoXmlDataProvider" (factory \c cargo-xml):
      validates, parses and builds the messages of XSD-defined cargo message families, such as UN/CEFACT
      Cross-Industry messages (schemas included) and IATA Cargo-XML
    - @ref cdadataproviderintro "CdaDataProvider" (factory \c cda): parses and validates
      HL7 CDA / HL7 v3 clinical documents, returning document metadata, sections and structured entries

    @section xmlusermoduleswebcontent Web Content

    @ref webcontentutilintro "WebContentUtil" provides web content processing: a parallel
    web crawler (@ref WebContentUtil::WebCrawler "WebCrawler") with SSRF protection
    (@ref WebContentUtil::SsrfFilter "SsrfFilter") and robots.txt support
    (@ref WebContentUtil::RobotsTxt "RobotsTxt"), sitemap parsing, URL normalization, HTML text extraction, text
    chunking and a local document reader.
*/
